<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: IAWS executive named president of GAFTA.</title>
<headline>IAWS executive named president of GAFTA.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>IAWS Group Plc said on Tuesday that Rory Toal, its executive director with responsibility for the group's animal feed business, has been elected president of the Grain &amp; Feed Trade Association (GAFTA).</p>
<p>GAFTA is a world-wide organisation promoting international trade in grains, animal feedstuffs, pulses and rice.</p>
<p>Toal succeeds the UK's David Small and will hold the post for an 18-month period, IAWS said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
